## What this predicate means

**A `requires` B** — applying or adhering to memorial A *requires* familiarity with / adherence to memorial B.  The dependency typed-edge: a protocol requires another protocol; a guidance requires a reference; an artifact requires a method specification.  Forms a **strict partial order** — strict because A requires B but B doesn't require A back (asymmetric), no memorial requires itself (irreflexive), and dependency composes transitively (A requires B + B requires C ⊨ A requires C).

